<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sardis</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sardis was the capital of the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydia">Lydia</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a> captured it in 546 BCE after defeating King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croesus">Croesus</a>, and it became a major Achaemenid administrative centre. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> profile, it was the western terminus of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-road">Royal Road</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sardis.jpg" alt="Sardis" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carole Raddato from FRANKFURT, Germany · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Bath-Gymnasium_complex_at_Sardis,_late_2nd_-_early_3rd_century_AD,_Sardis,_Turkey_(17098680002).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
